</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Countering Self-Preference Bias.</span>
A specific concern is that GPT-5 might over-rate GPT-5 responses. Our data refutes this. As seen in Figure <a href="#A5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix E Inter Judge agreement ‣ Beyond Refusal: Probing the Limits of Agentic Self-Correction for Semantic Sensitive Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, GPT-5 (Top Row) often reports <span id="S5.SS5.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lower</span> percentage reductions than smaller judges (e.g., Qwen-8B, Bottom Row). Thus, the advanced reasoning capabilities of GPT-5 make it a <span id="S5.SS5.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">stricter</span> grader, capable of detecting subtle leakage that smaller judges miss. Thus, our reported main results (Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experimental Setup ‣ Beyond Refusal: Probing the Limits of Agentic Self-Correction for Semantic Sensitive Information" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) likely represent a conservative lower bound on defense performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span><span id="S5.T5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation of Iterative Refinement (<span id="S5.T5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SemSIEdit</span>).</span> We track the evolution of privacy and utility metrics across the optimization loop (<math id="S5.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=3</annotation></semantics></math>). <span id="S5.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> indicates the best performance per model. Note that larger models (GPT-5) converge to optimal safety quickly (<math id="S5.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2</annotation></semantics></math>) with minimal utility loss.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T5.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:327.8pt;height:149.4pt;vertical-align:-72.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-62.1pt,28.3pt) scale(0.725286365871564,0.725286365871564) ;">
